        "id": "maxim:environmental-engineering:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "environmental-engineering",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "environmental-engineering",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Environmental Engineering - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**RCRA vs. CERCLA**: RCRA governs active waste management (prospective, compliance-oriented).\nCERCLA governs cleanup of historical releases (retrospective, liability-oriented). A site\ncan be subject to both — a RCRA-permitted facility that had historical releases triggering\nCERCLA liability. RCRA compliance does not provide CERCLA immunity."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#011",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:environmental-engineering:00-overview, git-history:environmental-engineering:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "environmental-engineering/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "environmental-engineering/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:environmental-engineering:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "environmental-engineering",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "environmental-engineering",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Environmental Engineering - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**SDWA vs. CWA**: SDWA protects drinking water (tap backward to intake). CWA protects\nreceiving water bodies from discharges. They work in sequence — CWA keeps source water\nclean enough that SDWA treatment is feasible and affordable."
    },
