        "title": "Environmental Engineering - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every environmental engineering calculation starts here. The mass balance equation is the **continuity equation** — the same conservation PDE that governs heat transfer (energy balance), electromagnetics (charge conservation), and fluid mechanics (Reynolds transport theorem). The form d(M)/dt = flux_in - flux_out + source is universal across physics and engineering; environmental engineering applies it to chemical species concentrations rather than energy or charge."
